  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Q-2 is a contract decision (high).</strong> The answered failure record says outcome error with no statistic key. The shipped record schemas accept success or failure only and require every statistic key. The plan stops at awaiting-input and recommends an additive schema change.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Two words for a failed outcome (medium).</strong> Calibration writes failure; the contract and the answer say error. Only option C of Q-2 unifies them.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Help text keeps growing (low).</strong> Later slices took the over-width count from 9 options to 47 lines. Step 1 applies a rule, and the widened test fails the gate if a later option makes a line longer than 80 columns.</aside>
  </div>
